### Why `useSyncExternalStore`

- The state lives outside React (in the browser), so this hook is a pure *subscription* — no `setState` in an effect, no stale-value tearing in concurrent rendering.
- It handles SSR/hydration correctly via `getServerSnapshot`.
- Cleanup is automatic: listeners are removed when the last consumer unmounts.

